From 6d50794f30a9c1f6147e274699e55bd6abf8a4ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude-sandbox <sandbox@local>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 10:37:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] mdblist: read watch history from /sync/watched

DTOs, the endpoint, and a paging client. Purely additive - nothing
consumes it yet, and the only existing file touched is the API interface,
by one added method.

The response is an object of four arrays with an offset/limit/has_more
block and no totals, so the client pages until has_more is false. A
missing pagination block is treated as the last page rather than as more,
since the alternative loops against a server that never says stop and
spends the daily budget doing it; a page ceiling backs that up.

All-or-nothing on failure: any failed page abandons the fetch and returns
null rather than a partial set. Partial watch history is worse than none,
because the missing rows read as "not watched" - which would clear badges
and resurrect finished episodes into next-up.

Confidence is uneven and the DTO KDoc says so. The season entry shape is
measured from a live account: the show is nested inside the season body,
season ids carry only tmdb so identity comes from that nested show, and
the entry timestamp is last_watched_at, not the season_watched_at that
appears on /sync/last_activities. The movie, show and episode shapes are
unobserved - the probed account had those arrays empty - so they are
modelled on the season convention and the playback endpoint, with every
field nullable and the episode entry tolerating the show nested or as a
sibling. A wrong guess yields an unmapped row, not a parse crash.

Six unit tests, the season fixture being the exact live payload.

Upstream: NuvioMedia/NuvioTV. MDBList API by linaspurinis.
